  "layersOrdersUiViewDescription": "It is a widget: it shows what the ViewModel gives it and passes on what the user does. QueryBuilder renders the loading, error and data states; the button calls a ViewModel method.",
  "layersOrdersUiViewModelDescription": "The part of the ViewModel that lives in the browser: query reads, command writes, state holds what the user changes and derived computes from them.",
  "layersOrdersPageDescription": "The other half of the ViewModel lives on the server: load fetches the data before rendering and an action receives the form. Throwing NotFound or Redirect decides which page is shown.",
  "layersOrdersModelDescription": "A piece of business data, immutable and without screen logic. Whatever travels in a query needs toJson and fromJson.",
  "layersOrdersDataRepositoryDescription": "An interface with an HTTP implementation. It turns the response into models and backend errors into what a page knows how to throw: NotFound or HttpError. Never a Redirect: where a signed-out user goes is the middleware's call.",
  "layersOrdersDataServiceDescription": "One client per backend, with no state or rules: it asks and returns the response as is. ThorHttpClient sets the timeout and reuses connections.",
  "layersOrdersDataInjectionDescription": "A middleware puts the repository on the request with a ContextKey. The same Group serves the real repository in production and a fake one in tests.",
  "layersOrdersDataTestsDescription": "With a fake repository the page is tested without network or backend: the test client makes the request and the response is checked.",
